WEBVTT

asr-000006
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:38.820
Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Good morning to everyone.

asr-000007
00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:45.860
Committee Secretary: The Finance Committee, Subcommittee H, would like to acknowledge the following resource persons.

asr-000008
00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:55.360
Committee Secretary: As acknowledged earlier by the Chair, we have Chairperson Jorella Maria Lala Gamboa Soto Antonio.

asr-000009
00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.320
Committee Secretary: Good morning.

asr-000010
00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.960
Committee Secretary: From the Movie and Television Review and Classification,

asr-000011
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:14.040
Committee Secretary: together with Mr. Roberto Diciembre, Antonio Ricardo Salomon, Jr., and Attorney Minowa Santo Domingo.

asr-000012
00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:27.080
Committee Secretary: From the Optical Media Board, we have Mr. Dennis Lorenzo Pinla, the Officer in Charge, Chairperson and Chief Executive Officer,

asr-000013
00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.980
Committee Secretary: together with Mr. Victorio.

asr-000014
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:46.460
Committee Secretary: From the Film Development Council of the Philippines, we have Mr. Jose Maria Socorro Javier Reyes, and Executive Director, Raysheld Villaluna.

asr-000015
00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:57.500
Committee Secretary: From the Philippine Racing Commission, we have Mr. Aurelio De Leon, and Mr. Ronald Porpoise.

asr-000016
00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.180
Committee Secretary: Good morning.

asr-000017
00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:05.180
Committee Secretary: From the Commission and Audit, for MTRCB, we have Mr. Amado Ablao.

asr-000018
00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:06.760
Committee Secretary: Good morning.

asr-000019
00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:15.180
Committee Secretary: From Optical Media Board, we have COA Optical Media Board, we have Marites Salamanya.

asr-000020
00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:16.480
Committee Secretary: Good morning.

asr-000021
00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:22.300
Committee Secretary: From COA FDCP, we have George Roman Lozano.

asr-000022
00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:23.180
Committee Secretary: Good morning.

asr-000023
00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:28.000
Committee Secretary: From COA Filracom, we have Mr. Amado Ablao.

asr-000024
00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:28.580
Committee Secretary: Good morning.

asr-000025
00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:35.180
Committee Secretary: From the Department of Budget and Management, for MTRCB, we have...

asr-000026
00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.300
Committee Secretary: Oh, wala pa siya.

asr-000027
00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.600
Committee Secretary: From FDCP, we have Ms. Evita Fontanilla.

asr-000028
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:42.760
Committee Secretary: Good morning.

asr-000029
00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.880
Committee Secretary: I think that is all for now, Mr. Chair.

asr-000030
00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Committee Secretary.

asr-000032
00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

asr-000033
00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:07.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As we begin our deliberations on the proposed budget or budgets of the Movie and Television Review and Classification Board,

asr-000034
00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:14.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: the Optical Media Board, the Film Development Council of the Philippines, and the Philippine Racing Commission,

asr-000035
00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:21.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I'd like to emphasize that these agencies may appear to operate in very different fields,

asr-000036
00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:27.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: but they share one important responsibility, protecting the public,

asr-000037
00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:34.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: interests while supporting industries that contribute to our economy, culture, and livelihood of our people.

asr-000038
00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ang budget po ng pamahalaan ay pera po ng taong bayan.

asr-000039
00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:39.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We all know that.

asr-000040
00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya sa bawat pisong ilalaan natin sa mga ahensya ninyo,

asr-000041
00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:51.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: dapat malinaw kung saan ito gagamitin, ano ang kongkretong resulta, at paano makikinabang ang ating mga kababayan.

asr-000042
00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:56.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Let's tackle, first, the budget of the MTRCB.

asr-000043
00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:57.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For MTRCB, we have...

asr-000051
00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:05.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For MTRCB, the agency was given under 2026 General Appropriations Act, a total budget of 75.29 million pesos.

asr-000052
00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:14.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 49.99 million.

asr-000053
00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:22.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Today, Filipinos are consuming content not only through traditional television and cinema,

asr-000054
00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: but also through streaming platforms and various digital channels.

asr-000055
00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:33.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Our children, in particular, have unprecedented access to content.

asr-000056
00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:38.320
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We, therefore, need to ask whether a regulatory framework is keeping pace with these changes.

asr-000057
00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:02.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Second, the Optical Media Board.

asr-000058
00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:11.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For OMB, the agency was given under the 2026 General Appropriations Act, a total budget of 47.03 million.

asr-000059
00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:18.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 53.462 million.

asr-000060
00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The media landscape has dramatically changed.

asr-000061
00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: CDs and DVDs...

asr-000062
00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:36.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We have moved into a digital environment where content can be copied, downloaded, distributed, streamed, and reproduced almost instantly.

asr-000063
00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: This raises an important question.

asr-000064
00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:46.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is the Optical Media Board still operating with the mandate and systems appropriate for today's digital economy?

asr-000065
00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:50.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We need to make sure that public funds are being used efficiently,

asr-000066
00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:57.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: that the agency is responding to actual threats to intellectual property and legitimate businesses.

asr-000067
00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Third, the Film Development Council of the Philippines.

asr-000068
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:11.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For FDCP, the agency was given under the 2026 General Appropriations Act, a total budget of 367.35 million pesos.

asr-000069
00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:19.460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 311.74.

asr-000070
00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:23.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The Philippine film industry is not merely an entertainment industry.

asr-000071
00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:27.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It is part of our cultural identity.

asr-000072
00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:34.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It is also a potential source of jobs, tourism, investment, and international recognition for Filipino talent.

asr-000073
00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:44.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We have Filipino filmmakers, actors, writers, directors, animators, cinematographers, editors, production workers, and other creative professionals

asr-000074
00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:49.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: who have demonstrated that we can compete internationally.

asr-000075
00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:56.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: But government support must translate into real opportunities for Filipino workers and filmmakers.

asr-000076
00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:03.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We should therefore examine how FDCP's program are benefiting independent filmmakers,

asr-000077
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:11.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: regional filmmakers, young artists, and emerging talents that only establish names in the industry.

asr-000078
00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:16.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Finally, the Philippine Racing Commission or FILRACOM.

asr-000079
00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:21.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For FILRACOM, the agency was given under the 2026 General Appropriations Act,

asr-000080
00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:26.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: a total budget of 199.76 million pesos.

asr-000082
00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:34.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 202.85 million pesos.

asr-000083
00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:38.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The horse racing industry is not simply about betting or entertainment.

asr-000084
00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:47.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It involves breeders, trainers, jockeys, veterinarians, farm workers, racetrack employees,

asr-000085
00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:51.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and thousands of families whose livelihoods are connected to the industry.

asr-000086
00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:55.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ibig sabihin po, nakapagbibigay po siya ng trabaho.

asr-000087
00:09:55.600 --> 00:10:00.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We therefore need to ensure that FILRACOM is effectively regulating the industry,

asr-000088
00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: protecting the integrity of horse racing,

asr-000089
00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:11.520
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and making sure that the government revenues generated from the sector are properly accounted for and maximized.

asr-000090
00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:18.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I would therefore like to know whether FILRACOM proposed budget is sufficient to strengthen regulation,

asr-000091
00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: improving monitoring, modernize its system,

asr-000092
00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:28.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and ensure transparency in the collection and utilization of racing revenues.

asr-000096
00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:33.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: These four agencies operate in different sectors, but they face a common challenge.

asr-000097
00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:38.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The world is changing faster than our regulatory and support systems.

asr-000098
00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:43.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Horse racing is becoming more technologically driven.

asr-000099
00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:47.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Media piracy is becoming increasingly digital.

asr-000100
00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:52.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Television and film consumption are moving toward online platforms.

asr-000101
00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:58.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And the creative economy is becoming increasingly global.

asr-000107
00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:04.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Therefore, our budget deliberation should not simply ask how much money does the agency need.

asr-000108
00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:08.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We should ask more important questions like,

asr-000109
00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:15.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: what will the Filipino people get in return for the budget given to you?

asr-000110
00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:19.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Every allocation must have a corresponding public benefit.

asr-000111
00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:24.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We need stronger accountability, measurable outcomes, efficient use of resources,

asr-000112
00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:32.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and programs that directly benefit Filipino workers, consumers, artists, and entrepreneurs.

asr-000113
00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:36.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: At the end of the day, ang budget po ay hindi lamang numero sa papel,

asr-000114
00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:41.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: buhay, trabaho at serbisyo publiko ang nakasalalay dito.

asr-000115
00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:47.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya ngayong deliberasyon, I look forward to hearing from your agencies,

asr-000116
00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:53.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: your respective offices, their concrete plans, their accomplishments, their challenges,

asr-000117
00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:58.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and most importantly, how they intend to ensure that every peso entrusted to them

asr-000118
00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:02.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: by the Filipino people will be put to good use.

asr-000119
00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000120
00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:21.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay, on that note, let us proceed with the briefing proper.

asr-000121
00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:22.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For the orderly procedure,

asr-000122
00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:26.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: we will have the following chronology of budget presentation.

asr-000123
00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:30.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: First to present is the Movie and Television Review Classification Board,

asr-000124
00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:35.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: MTRCB, followed by the OMB Optical Media Board,

asr-000125
00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:38.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: then the Film Development Council of the Philippines,

asr-000126
00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:41.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and last, the Philippine Racing Commission, or FILRACOM.

asr-000127
00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We will open the floor for queries or questions

asr-000128
00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:48.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: after each presentation of the aforementioned agencies.

asr-000129
00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:51.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We now recognize Chairperson Lala Soto Antonio

asr-000130
00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:57.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: for the presentation of MTRCB's proposed budget for Fiscal Year 2027.

asr-000131
00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:00.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ma'am, please proceed with your presentation.

asr-000132
00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Senator Erwin Tulfo, thank you.

asr-000133
00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: To all who are present here today,

asr-000134
00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:09.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: it is my honor to present to you the proposed budget

asr-000135
00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:12.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: of the Movie and Television Review and Classification Board

asr-000136
00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:16.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for Fiscal Year 2027.

asr-000137
00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The total proposed budget

asr-000138
00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:23.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for Fiscal Year 2027 amounts to

asr-000139
00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:28.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: $197,898,000.

asr-000140
00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:33.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Of this, only $53.39 million

asr-000141
00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:35.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for personal services

asr-000142
00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:38.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: will be sourced from the national government,

asr-000143
00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:43.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: while the larger share of $144.51 million,

asr-000144
00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:45.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Mr. Chairman,

asr-000145
00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: will be through the agencies' generated income.

asr-000146
00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:53.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The graph shows the proposed budget

asr-000147
00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:57.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for Fiscal Year 2027 by allotment case

asr-000148
00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: with a total of $197,898,000.

asr-000149
00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The personal services amounting to $53.39 million

asr-000150
00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:09.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: comprises 27% of the total budget

asr-000151
00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:12.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: that is sourced from the national government.

asr-000152
00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:15.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The remaining 73% for the maintenance

asr-000153
00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:19.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: and other operating expenses and the capital outlay

asr-000154
00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: amounting to $144.51 million

asr-000155
00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:26.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: again is sourced from the agencies' collected income.

asr-000156
00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The graph shows the proposed budget

asr-000157
00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:34.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for Fiscal Year 2027 by appropriation source

asr-000158
00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:39.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: with a total of $197,898,000.

asr-000159
00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:43.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The agencies specific for personal services

asr-000160
00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: amounting to $49.99 million

asr-000161
00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: comprises the 25.1 million

asr-000162
00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:51.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: and 25.26% of the total budget,

asr-000163
00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:55.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: while the 1.72% of which will be

asr-000164
00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:59.480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for the retirement and life insurance premium

asr-000165
00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:01.400
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: GSIS.

asr-000166
00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:19.020
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The remaining 73.02% will be sourced in the Special Account in the General Fund or the Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses and the Capital Outlay amounting to 144.51 million.

asr-000167
00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:39.020
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: For 2027, the total proposed budget for Capital Outlay amounts to 35.78 million allocated for ICT software and equipment or the year-to-implementation of the redevelopment of a transact and collection system of the MTRCB.

asr-000168
00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:48.760
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: As of July 31, 2026, the book balance of our sinking fund amounts to

asr-000169
00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:58.700
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: 641,412,719.08 centavos.

asr-000170
00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:16.820
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: For the budget utilization rate, from 2020 to 2025, the MTRCB steadily improved its budget utilization with obligation rates rising from 70.23% in 2020

asr-000171
00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:23.390
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: to a peak of 97.72% in 2023,

asr-000173
00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:44.300
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Before settling at 95.31% in 2024 and 86.92% in 2025, disbursement efficiency has also strengthened, reaching 93.16% in 2025, underscoring effective fund release and program execution.

asr-000175
00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:57.700
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The agency received significantly larger allotment of 267.67 million.

asr-000176
00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:09.040
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Of this, 110,175,000 has been obligated, reflecting a 41.16% obligation rate.

asr-000177
00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:18.720
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Disbursement remains strong at 98.68 million, or 89.57%, sustaining the MTRCB.

asr-000178
00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:23.840
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The agency's record of efficient fund release once obligations are made.

asr-000179
00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:37.420
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: This mid-year performance highlights continued strength in disbursement efficiency, with obligations expected to accelerate in the latter half of the year, to align with the increased allocation.

asr-000180
00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:47.960
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: For the financial performance, fiscal year 2025, the table shows the financial performance of the MTRCB for 2025.

asr-000181
00:17:48.720 --> 00:18:10.220
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: From 176.06 million, allotment received 86.93%, or 153.05 million of it was obligated, and 93.17% or 143.59 million was disbursed for fiscal year 2025.

asr-000182
00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:18.720
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The unobligated allotment, amounting to 22.419 million, was moved as a continuing allocation.

asr-000183
00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:32.100
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The unpaid obligations, amounting to 10.459 million, was recorded as accounts payable and paid during the first quarter of fiscal year 2025.

asr-000184
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:41.840
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The table above shows the financial performance of the MTRCB as of June 30, 2026.

asr-000185
00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:47.740
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: From the 267.67 million allotment received,

asr-000186
