asr-000687
00:55:40.320 --> 00:56:10.300
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: [unclear] We will be presenting a short briefing on what transpired during the Optical Media Board. Okay, first slide please. As we all know, the Optical Media Board was created under Republic Act 9239, in which the OMB is mandated to promote the protection of intellectual property rights, specifically copyright, by regulating the mastering, manufacturing, importing, exporting, distribution and selling of optical and magnetic media.

asr-000688
00:56:10.320 --> 00:56:40.300
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: When we say magnetic media, ito rin po yung mga, ano, yung mga hard disk drive na nasa computer natin, as well as its technical variations thereof. Okay. The vision of the Optical Media Board is an economy which is free from optical media piracy, wherein there is a level playing field for all legitimate players. Of course, our mission is to promote and protect intellectual property in digital form.

asr-000689
00:56:40.320 --> 00:57:10.300
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: At present, the OMB?s mandate is sixfold. First is the permits and licenses. Second, we are also empowered to conduct proactive inspections, and to act as complainant, and to hear and resolve administrative cases, and create and maintain a database of licensed media and establishments, as well as establish support offices when necessary. For our fiscal performance as of last year,

asr-000690
00:57:10.320 --> 00:57:40.300
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: for the allotment received, we have a grand total of 73,302,000. Obligations incurred were 56,280,000. Disbursements were 53,749,000, wherein the percentage of obligations is 76.78% and the percentage of disbursement is 95.50%.

asr-000691
