01:03:13.540 --> 01:03:15.440
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: And for the historical standing...

asr-000755
01:03:16.280 --> 01:03:35.420
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: As seen here, on February 21, 2021, then-honorable Sen. Jean-Claude Estrada has filed a bill seeking the abolishment of the Optical Media Board and the transfer of our powers to the FTCP.

asr-000756
01:03:35.420 --> 01:04:04.920
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Likewise, on January 5, 2026, nagkaroon po ng special session po dito for the winding down, and on January 8, 2026, then Sen. Gatchalian, who's now our Senate President, has proposed for the abolition of the OMB and a transfer of our functions to the Intellectual Property Office.

asr-000757
01:04:05.420 --> 01:04:32.420
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Hence, on February 11, we had conducted a Committee on Public Information and Mass Media, and on February 23, we have already established our Change Management and Placement Team in order to know our future of our employees po.

asr-000758
01:04:33.460 --> 01:04:34.420
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: And on...

asr-000759
01:04:35.420 --> 01:04:51.620
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: On May, we have also conducted several meetings with our FTCP counterparts, with the Civil Service, as well as with the DBM, in order to ensure the smooth transition of our employees on that matter.

asr-000760
01:04:52.500 --> 01:05:02.640
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: And on June, as of this year, on June 2, we have met with the DBM on that part regarding our winding down po.

asr-000761
01:05:04.260 --> 01:05:05.340
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Last slide po.

asr-000762
01:05:05.420 --> 01:05:25.400
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: On the agency's winding down plan, from February up to June of 2026 review, it was stated that the agency's, the CMPT of the agency proposed for the abolition of the office.

asr-000763
01:05:26.840 --> 01:05:34.500
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Because we know or recognize that we cannot, we are limited in our powers to curb physical...

asr-000764
01:05:34.500 --> 01:05:49.360
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: ...digital piracy under our current laws, kasi po, ang alam po ninyo, aside that the Optical Media Board, which our predecessor was the VRB, dati po, if everybody knows, si dati po, bete maksasaka VHS po.

asr-000765
01:05:49.920 --> 01:05:53.700
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Tapos nung nagkaroon ng mga CDs, inamend po ng law, naging OMB.

asr-000766
01:05:53.960 --> 01:05:54.700
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Now, as we all know, this is a digital format, that's why we recognize that we are severely restricted in our...

asr-000767
01:05:54.700 --> 01:06:03.580
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: ...digital piracy under our current laws, kasi po, alam po ninyo, aside that the Optical Media Board, which our predecessor was the VRB, dati po, if everybody knows, si dati po, bete maksasaka VHS po.

asr-000768
01:06:03.580 --> 01:06:08.260
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Now, as we all know, this is a digital format, that's why we recognize that we are severely restricted in our law, nakakahinder po sa performance namin yung batas namin po.

asr-000769
01:06:10.060 --> 01:06:23.420
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: So, for that, for our personnel, we have a permanent staff physician, because out of the 93 positions, we have 45 warm bodies in our office.

asr-000770
01:06:24.160 --> 01:06:29.980
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: And we have also around 10 job orders to assist us in our daily-to-day functions.

asr-000771
01:06:31.460 --> 01:06:33.560
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: Right now, we are...

asr-000772
01:06:33.580 --> 01:06:42.800
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: While we had talked with the DBM personnel last week, we are awaiting the recommendations, and of course, well, since...

asr-000773
01:06:42.800 --> 01:06:46.780
