Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you.

asr-000836
01:11:05.580 --> 01:11:06.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you.

asr-000837
01:11:06.580 --> 01:11:07.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you po.

asr-000838
01:11:07.580 --> 01:11:08.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Director.

asr-000839
01:11:10.580 --> 01:11:14.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Done with your presentation, Sir Dennis.

asr-000840
01:11:15.580 --> 01:11:20.580
OMB OIC Chairperson Dennis Lorenzo B. Pinlac: I think our chief from the admin would like to add also a comment.

asr-000841
01:11:20.580 --> 01:11:21.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Go ahead po.

asr-000842
01:11:21.580 --> 01:11:22.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair.

asr-000843
01:11:22.580 --> 01:11:29.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: Before we end our presentation, Mr. Chair, beyond our day-to-day operations and budget proposals,

asr-000844
01:11:29.580 --> 01:11:30.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: we must respectfully place on record the agency's pressing operations,

asr-000846
01:11:31.580 --> 01:11:38.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: and administrative concerns regarding the special provisions mentioned earlier on the winding down of the optical

asr-000847
01:11:38.580 --> 01:11:43.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: media board under the FY 2026.

asr-000848
01:11:43.580 --> 01:11:47.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: While the FOA 2026 appropriate at 47 million earmark exclusively for winding down operations,

asr-000849
01:11:47.580 --> 01:11:56.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: This provision has placed the agency in extraordinary operational and legal Limbo.

asr-000850
01:11:56.580 --> 01:11:59.580
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: While the special provisions directs the winding down of the agency,

asr-000851
01:11:59.580 --> 01:12:29.160
OMB Administrative Chief Janine Joyce G. Sison: The Republic Act No. 9239 remains substantive, unrepealed law. The pending abolition measures, Senate Bills 991 and 1654, are still pending in the legislative mill. As demonstrated by our frontline data, piracy and illicit hardware importations have not disappeared. They have modernized. In 2026 alone, our team conducted over 1,850 inspections and collected nearly 30 million in revenue.

asr-000852
01:12:29.580 --> 01:12:45.060
